  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "In {Asia} , messaging {platforms} are growing rapidly, with {users} in the {hundreds} of millions.The global messaging {market} is bustling with Apps that {differ} in functions.Influenced by increasing {Internet} connectivity, as the {height} of {mobile phone} usage reaches new levels, the popularity of these platforms is {spreading globally} .Consequently, emojis also have gained a {decent} following around the world.It's been reported that 76 {percent} of {employees} in some Western countries are using emojis at work.",
      "cn": "在 亚洲 ，信息 平台 发展迅速， 用户 数量达数亿之多。全球信息 市场 上充斥着各种功能各 异 的应用程序。受 互联网 的连通性不断提高的影响，随着 移动电话 使用率达到新 高 ，这些平台的受欢迎程度在 全球范围内传播 开来。因此，表情符号在世界各地也拥有了 相当数量的 使用者。据报道，在一些西方国家， 百分之 七十六的 员工 在工作中会使用表情符号。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Nowadays, companies use messaging apps for {customer} support, real-time {updates} , and {internal} communications.A large number of the working population relies on them to stay connected with colleagues and {clients} and {hide} their personal lives through custom {profiles} .However, written communications can often seem {pale} or {thin} .Cultural differences in writing style or {tone} could also lead to misunderstandings.While some may {dismiss} emojis as informal, they offer several {superb} benefits when used thoughtfully.Using emojis can add humor and feeling, making it {convenient} to ensure the message is clear.For instance, WhatsApp's {handbag} stickers and Telegram's customizable ( (可定制的) ) {panda} icons are popular choices among chatters.Messages with emojis feel more {conversational} , {encouraging} better and more frequent communication.",
      "cn": "如今，各个公司会使用信息应用程序来提供 客户 支持、实时 更新 和 内部 沟通。大量职场人士借助这些应用程序与同事和 客户 保持联系，并通过自定义 简介隐藏 自己的个人生活。然而，书面交流往往显得 平淡 而 单薄 。不同文化背景下的写作风格或 语气 上的差异也可能导致误解。虽然有些人可能会认为表情符号不够正式而 不予理会 ，但如果使用得当，它们能带来诸多 显著的 益处。使用表情符号可以增加幽默感和感情色彩，从而 便 于确保信息清晰明了。例如，WhatsApp的 手提包 贴纸和Telegram的可定制 熊猫 图标都是聊天者的热门选择。带有表情符号的信息更 有对话感 ，能 促进 更好、更 频繁的 交流。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "In any given office, employees can range from age twenty-two to {seventy} and beyond.An easy way to bring all work generations together is with a chat platform, where physical {borders} no longer limit our interactions.While the younger generations prefer to communicate {visually} , for those used to working with traditional {tools} like email, it may feel like a {learning} curve ( (曲线) ), making them somehow {pessimistic} about the outcomes.The good news is that it's simple to learn and can be worth the effort.",
      "cn": "在任何一间办公室里，员工的年龄范围可能下至22岁，上至 70 岁甚至更大。将不同年龄段的员工凝聚在一起的一个简单方法就是使用聊天平台，在这些平台上，物理 边界 不再限制我们的交流。虽然年轻一代更喜欢 可视化 交流，但对于那些更习惯使用电子邮件等传统 工具 的人来说，这些平台的使用体验可能就像一条 学习 曲线，这让他们在某种程度上对结果感到 悲观 。好在这些工具学起来简单，值得付出一番努力。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "Emojis can act as a {quick} shortcut to enhance efficiency.They help emphasize key points and {resolve} confusion.For example, a thumbs-up emoji can quickly show that you {approve} of a {proposal} or {suggestion} ; an {arrow} might be used to {outline} the next steps in a project.",
      "cn": "表情符号可以成为一种 快速 的捷径来提高效率。它们有助于突出重点、 解决 困惑。例如，一个竖起大拇指的表情符号可以迅速表明你 赞同 一项 提议 或 建议 ；一个 箭头 符号可以用来 概括 一个项目的下一步计划。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "There is also the matter of tone.Who hasn't received an annoying email that {ruined} an entire day? Even a {formal} email can seem cold and {unfriendly} .Emojis can help communication feel friendlier, and even a serious note can be {softened} with an encouraging smile.",
      "cn": "还有语气方面的问题。谁没有收到过一封烦人的电子邮件，结果一整天（的好心情）都被 毁掉 了呢。即使是一封 正式 的电子邮件也会显得冷漠且 不友好 。表情符号可以让沟通显得更友好，即使是一条严肃的信息也可以用一个鼓励的微笑符号来 缓和 语气。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "Studies show that friendlier communication leads to a happier {workplace} .Friendly emojis can {depress} the negative impact of formal barriers often associated with {corporate} environments, creating a more inclusive atmosphere.When your employees begin adding smiling emojis to their {business} communication, you'll know you have succeeded in improving your work {culture} .",
      "cn": "研究表明，更友好的沟通有助于营造更快乐的 工作环境 。友好的表情符号可以 减少 通常与 企业 环境相关的那种正式隔阂的负面影响，营造出一种更具包容性的氛围。当你的员工开始在他们的 业务 沟通中添加微笑表情符号时，你就知道你已经成功地改善了工作 文化 。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP4m+378Hw1xTRxUdPaP/PFjKUFq4K2G7tp6ZLYoCE601yW1W39VMdLmovFdSHs4nVQ=="
    }
  ],
